        "answer": {
          "short": "$36\\text{ u}^2$",
          "worked": "$$(2x+1)-(x^2+2x-8)=9-x^2.$$\nHence the two integrals are equal.\n$$\\begin{aligned}A&=\\int_{-3}^{3}(9-x^2)\\,dx\\\\&=\\left[9x-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_{-3}^{3}\\\\&=(27-9)-(-27+9)\\\\&=36\\text{ u}^2\\end{aligned}$$",
